# `load existing game` navigates to the save selector.
#
# **The saves screen lists one row per save**, which is the same shape as `configure` listing one
# row per size. **A save carries its turn**, because `load previous turn` needs something to select
# from and `{save}` is where it lives.

{test name:load-existing-game-goes-to-the-saves-screen}

{given}
{screen name:menu}
{save name:first-game turn:3} -> 1

{when}
{load-existing-game}

{then}
{screen name:saves}
{save name:first-game turn:3} -> 1
{item of:saves name:start active:0} -> 1
{item of:saves name:back active:1} -> 1
{attention of:first-game}
